 ## Overview
-Region Adaptive Hierarchical Transform (RAHT) is a bottom-up wavelet transform that reorganizes color or scalar attributes along an octree structure by pairing neighboring voxels to produce low-frequency (DC) and high-frequency coefficients [S1]. It sets itself apart from graph-based transforms by relying on simple pairwise operations rather than costly eigen-decompositions, making it computationally efficient and suitable for real-time compression of attributes with strong local correlation [S1].
+Region Adaptive Hierarchical Transform (RAHT) is a bottom-up transform that reorganizes color or scalar attributes along an octree by pairing neighboring voxels to produce low-frequency (DC) and high-frequency coefficients [S1]. It distinguishes itself from graph-based transforms by relying on simple pairwise operations rather than costly eigen-decompositions, making it computationally efficient and suitable for real-time compression of attributes with strong local correlation [S1].
 
 ## How it works
